      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh of course, base on the doc (go/roboStrictMode).\nWe have implemented strict_mode for Robolectric to enforcing developers writing multivalent tests. In strict_mode, no Robolectric API invocation are allowed, e.g.: \nshadowOf(context.getPackageManager())\n        .setSystemFeature(PackageManager.FEATURE_NFC, /* supported\u003d */ true);\nUnfortunately, there are still many existing Robolectric tests that had to use some Robolectric API more or less. \nThis is the main reason that we are massively opting out these tests manually as `strict_mode: false`. Next step will be making all Robolectric test by default as \"strict_mode: true\"",
